      "description": "Kodist is a point-and-shoot camera that produce lifelike film photography shots.\n\n◎ No AI Enhancements\n\nKodist avoids all AI enhancements by processing data directly from the sensors:\n\n- Your shots are never too evenly lit\n- There's no excessive sharpening, aggressive denoising, and artificial smudging\n- No weird, frowned-upon HDR artifacts on object edges\n- Natural and pleasant-looking grains produces by physics, not by an algorithm\n\n◎ Film Photography Profiles\n\nYour shots are rendered with your choice of a professional film photography colour profile. They produce natural and balance colours that makes your shots stand out in the sea of phone photographs. \n\n◎ Photos in 1 Step\n\nPoint and shoot, and that's it: your photo is saved to your iOS Photo Library, and the camera gets out of your way.\n\n◎ Minimal App, Packed Technologies\n\nKodist is minimally featured, but user experience is not an afterthought.\n\n- 10-bit HEIF support saves your photos in a rich, space-efficient format\n- Geotagging makes your photos searchable on maps in your Photo Library\n- Automatic image orientation allows your to take photos however you hold the phone\n- Photos are saved to iOS Photo Library with full EXIF info. There's no separate in-app album\n\n◎ Free (for now)\n\nThere are no pay-to-unlock features (yet!) and you can keep having fun for free. Tips are welcome and we may have something for you in the future ;)",
